    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0630" n="592" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg592"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/5371: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-19T19:00:00+01:00">June 19, 1919—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:42 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2651. [From Lansing.] For your information. Referring to Mission’s number 2562 of
                    June 13th, 1919.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d266-f1"/> Treaty with Germany in final
                    form released in full to press this afternoon for publication Friday
                        morning<anchor n="49a" xml:id="d266-f2"/> in accordance with decision by
                    Council of Principal Allied and Associated Powers to publish at earliest
                    possible date after release <pb facs="0631" n="593" xml:id="pg593"/> of German
                    counter proposal and reply thereto. Ten copies of proof copy, first print, of
                    final treaty forwarded you by courier this afternoon. Additional copies will be
                    sent as soon as obtained. Lansing.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
